{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game genre game genre","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","fileName":"Game Genre.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Genre","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Design Methods]] · [[Video Game Genres and Platforms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Video Game Genres and Platforms","Game Mechanic","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game genre game genre","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","fileName":"Game Genre.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Genre","heading":"Game Genre","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game genre is a heuristic label for a familiar cluster of dominant gameplay and interaction conventions. It lets designers and players quickly anticipate likely mechanics and experiences.\n\nBecause the label compresses many distinct qualities, it can encourage lazy design or hide important differences. Describing specific [[Game Mechanic|mechanics]], timescales, and player activities gives a more precise account than relying on genre alone.\n\nThe source defines genre chiefly through characteristic kinds of challenges, regardless of setting or visual content. A familiar genre lowers communication and design risk by supplying expected actions, while a hybrid deliberately combines challenge patterns from more than one genre.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Video Game Genres and Platforms","Game Mechanic","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game genre game genre","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Genre.md","fileName":"Game Genre.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Genre","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Video Game Genres and Platforms","Game Mechanic","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}